{"schema_version":1,"run_id":"p4-setc-full-r1","system":"full","paper_id":"2212.06322v1","variant":"original","error_class":"method_mismatch","anchor":{"kind":"document"},"target":{"kind":"setting","key":"method"},"state":"verified_flag","summary":"The paper specifies MSE as the loss function for all experiments, but the codebase uses cross-entropy (Classification loss) for classification training.","evidence":[{"kind":"quote","source":{"kind":"submission","id":"2212.06322v1","title":null,"url":null},"text":"For all the experiments, Mean Squared Error (MSE) is used as the loss function, and SGD [61] is used as the optimizer with a learning rate of 0.1, and an L2 regularization with a weight of 0.0002.","page":null,"char_start":null,"char_end":null,"path":null,"line_start":null,"line_end":null},{"kind":"code","source":{"kind":"repository","id":"https://github.com/gaow0007/ATSPrivacy@b9bf5da58d515167f94d859e256fd8b18d8a1f7c","title":null,"url":"https://github.com/gaow0007/ATSPrivacy"},"text":"class Classification(Loss):\n    \"\"\"A classical NLL loss for classification. Evaluation has the softmax baked in.\n\n    The minimized criterion is cross entropy, the actual metric is total accuracy.\n    \"\"\"","page":null,"char_start":null,"char_end":null,"path":"inversefed/data/loss.py","line_start":86,"line_end":90}],"finding_id":"code-74155701fb1c4095-f0","severity":"high","duplicate_of":null}
{"schema_version":1,"run_id":"p4-setc-full-r1","system":"full","paper_id":"2212.06322v1","variant":"original","error_class":"method_mismatch","anchor":{"kind":"document"},"target":{"kind":"setting","key":"method"},"state":"verified_flag","summary":"The paper evaluates privacy leakage via membership inference attacks, whereas the code implements image reconstruction attacks from gradients using inversefed.GradientReconstructor.","evidence":[{"kind":"quote","source":{"kind":"submission","id":"2212.06322v1","title":null,"url":null},"text":"The adversary performs a membership inference attack on the trained model to try to identify samples that were present in the training data.","page":null,"char_start":null,"char_end":null,"path":null,"line_start":null,"line_end":null},{"kind":"code","source":{"kind":"repository","id":"https://github.com/gaow0007/ATSPrivacy@b9bf5da58d515167f94d859e256fd8b18d8a1f7c","title":null,"url":"https://github.com/gaow0007/ATSPrivacy"},"text":"    rec_machine = inversefed.GradientReconstructor(model, (dm, ds), config, num_images=num_images)\n    if opt.data == 'cifar100':\n        shape = (3, 32, 32)\n    elif opt.data == 'FashionMinist':\n        shape = (1, 32, 32)\n\n    if opt.rlabel:\n        output, stats = rec_machine.reconstruct(input_gradient, None, img_shape=shape) # reconstruction label\n    else:\n        output, stats = rec_machine.reconstruct(input_gradient, labels, img_shape=shape) # specify label","page":null,"char_start":null,"char_end":null,"path":"benchmark/cifar100_attack.py","line_start":91,"line_end":100}],"finding_id":"code-74155701fb1c4095-f1","severity":"high","duplicate_of":null}
{"schema_version":1,"run_id":"p4-setc-full-r1","system":"full","paper_id":"2212.06322v1","variant":"original","error_class":"method_mismatch","anchor":{"kind":"document"},"target":{"kind":"setting","key":"method"},"state":"verified_flag","summary":"The paper specifies using a custom semi-sigmoid activation function (ReLU(x) - ReLU(x - 1)) for all layers of LeNet, while the codebase uses standard nn.Sigmoid.","evidence":[{"kind":"quote","source":{"kind":"submission","id":"2212.06322v1","title":null,"url":null},"text":"For the MNIST dataset, we also evaluated the methods on the LeNet-5 [62] architecture in which the dimension of the feature embeddings is 120.","page":null,"char_start":null,"char_end":null,"path":null,"line_start":null,"line_end":null},{"kind":"code","source":{"kind":"repository","id":"https://github.com/gaow0007/ATSPrivacy@b9bf5da58d515167f94d859e256fd8b18d8a1f7c","title":null,"url":"https://github.com/gaow0007/ATSPrivacy"},"text":"    def __init__(self, num_classes=10, num_channels=3):\n        \"\"\"3-Layer sigmoid Conv with large linear layer.\"\"\"\n        super().__init__()\n        act = nn.Sigmoid\n        self.body = nn.Sequential(\n            nn.Conv2d(num_channels, 12, kernel_size=5, padding=5 // 2, stride=2),\n            act(),\n            nn.Conv2d(12, 12, kernel_size=5, padding=5 // 2, stride=2),\n            act(),\n            nn.Conv2d(12, 12, kernel_size=5, padding=5 // 2, stride=1),\n            act(),\n        )","page":null,"char_start":null,"char_end":null,"path":"inversefed/nn/models.py","line_start":306,"line_end":317}],"finding_id":"code-74155701fb1c4095-f2","severity":"high","duplicate_of":null}
